\f1\b\fs24 \cf2 How to use:
\f0\b0 \cf0 \
\
Put this script in your iTunes Scripts folder. This is located in \cf3 home > Library > iTunes\cf0 . If there is no folder named "Scripts" there, create one and put the script in it. It will then appear in iTunes' Script Menu, where you can select it by clicking on its name.\
\
Run the script. If you have an iPod mounted, you will be given the choice of searching for "one-hits" on the iPod or in iTunes. After several moments (the length of operation depends on the size of your library), the "One Hit Wonders" playlist will be selected, filled with the tracks that were collected.\
\

\f1\b \cf2 Also:
\f0\b0 \cf0 \
\
The script is fairly well commented so that you can edit it yourself. Double-click on it in the Finder and it will open in Script Editor. After making any changes, press 
\f1\b Command-S
\f0\b0  or choose "Save" in Script Editor's File menu.\
\
\'a5 If you want to change the name of the playlist, look for this line near the beginning of the script:\
\
\pard\tx160\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\li180\ql\qnatural

